Widget Tree

You already saw this briefly.

Suppose we have:

Scaffold(
  body: Column(
    children: [
      Text('Hello'),
      ElevatedButton(
        onPressed: () {},
        child: Text('Click'),
      ),
    ],
  ),
)

The structure is roughly:

Scaffold
   ↓
 Column
   ├── Text
   └── ElevatedButton
          ↓
        Text

This hierarchy is called the Widget Tree.

Each widget describes one part of the UI or its structure. 

“The Widget Tree describes the structure and hierarchy of the UI. It shows how widgets are nested inside other widgets.”

For example:

Scaffold
   ↓
 Column
   ├── Text
   └── Button

That's enough. You don't need a complicated definition.